{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":122304,"name":"Joanna Jablonski","username":"jojablonski","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/jojablonski/{size}/3159_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-20T13:13:46.611Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHere’s a new PEP that proposes how the Python Documentation Editorial Board will work:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0732/\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/2X/8/88d4484552c4beac33d9a0848f523aaa66aad78c.png\" class=\"site-icon\" data-dominant-color=\"979F6B\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0732/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003epeps.python.org\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0732/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePEP 732 – The Python Documentation Editorial Board | peps.python.org\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003ePython Enhancement Proposals (PEPs)\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAny feedback on this PEP would be appreciated.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2023-10-20T13:14:04.634Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1037,"reads":178,"readers_count":177,"score":5300.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":36710,"topic_slug":"pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board","display_username":"Joanna Jablonski","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0732/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 732 – The Python Documentation Editorial Board | peps.python.org","clicks":156}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":9}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":3061,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board/36710/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":9}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":9,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":122342,"name":"Jacob Goldsmith","username":"jacgoldsm","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/a183cd/{size}.png","created_at":"2023-10-20T15:41:28.271Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIs \u003ca href=\"http://docs.python.org\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003edocs.python.org\u003c/a\u003e \u003cem\u003ecpython\u003c/em\u003e documentation or \u003cem\u003epython\u003c/em\u003e documentation? I’ve always thought of it as the latter, though cpython has pride of place as the reference implementation.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2023-10-20T15:41:28.271Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":173,"readers_count":172,"score":59.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":36710,"topic_slug":"pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board","display_username":"Jacob Goldsmith","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://docs.python.org","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"3.12.0 Documentation","clicks":5}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":13384,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board/36710/2","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":122345,"name":"Ned Batchelder","username":"nedbat","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/nedbat/{size}/8744_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-20T15:56:45.995Z","cooked":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIs \u003ca href=\"http://docs.python.org\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003edocs.python.org \u003c/a\u003e \u003cem\u003ecpython\u003c/em\u003e documentation or \u003cem\u003epython\u003c/em\u003e documentation?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a great question.  In truth, it’s both. Implementation details (CPython-specific) are called out, but perhaps not as uniformly as they could be.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAre there particular issues you’re seeing with that tension?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2023-10-20T15:56:45.995Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":167,"readers_count":166,"score":48.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":36710,"topic_slug":"pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board","display_username":"Ned Batchelder","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://docs.python.org","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"3.12.0 Documentation","clicks":2}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"reply_to_user":{"id":13384,"username":"jacgoldsm","name":"Jacob Goldsmith","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/a183cd/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1093,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board/36710/3","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":122445,"name":"Terry Jan Reedy","username":"tjreedy","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/tjreedy/{size}/137_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-21T04:35:23.424Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThe Python 3.x Reference is intended to define the Python 3.x language.  Anything specific to CPython, such as ‘object ID = address’, should be noted as such.  The PyPY implementation, in particular, forced some clarifications on what was ‘Python’ and what was specifically CPython.  Any other implementation should describes \u003cem\u003eits\u003c/em\u003e specializations and deviations.  The Library Manual describes what come with CPython.  Other implementations are at least encouraged to include everything not CPython specific.  The C-API is obviously C specific.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2023-10-21T04:35:23.424Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":145,"readers_count":144,"score":89.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":36710,"topic_slug":"pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board","display_username":"Terry Jan Reedy","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":4}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":110,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board/36710/4","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":4}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":4,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":122448,"name":"Hugo van Kemenade","username":"hugovk","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/hugovk/{size}/14505_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-21T05:55:13.657Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThank you for working on this! I’m +1 for both the PEP and the initial list of members.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe motivation section introduces the Working Group but not the Editorial Board. Could we have a single sentence explaining the relationship between the WG and the EB? For example, this is the EB of the WG.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is partially explained by the diagram. For accessibility, it would help to add such a sentence in the body text, and/or something as alt text.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2023-10-21T05:55:13.657Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":135,"readers_count":134,"score":62.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":36710,"topic_slug":"pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board","display_username":"Hugo van Kemenade","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":358,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board/36710/5","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":122621,"name":"Carol Willing","username":"willingc","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/willingc/{size}/20_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-22T14:10:26.930Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eGreat question \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/jacgoldsm\"\u003e@jacgoldsm\u003c/a\u003e. The Scope section of the PEP clarifies that \u003ca href=\"http://docs.python.org\"\u003edocs.python.org\u003c/a\u003e is covered by this PEP. \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/apple/smile.png?v=12\" title=\":smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2023-10-22T14:10:26.930Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":116,"readers_count":115,"score":38.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":36710,"topic_slug":"pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board","display_username":"Carol Willing","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://docs.python.org","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"3.12.0 Documentation","clicks":3}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"reply_to_user":{"id":13384,"username":"jacgoldsm","name":"Jacob Goldsmith","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/a183cd/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":14,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board/36710/6","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":122807,"name":"Joanna Jablonski","username":"jojablonski","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/jojablonski/{size}/3159_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-23T14:16:56.126Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/hugovk\"\u003e@hugovk\u003c/a\u003e Thanks for highlighting that we have a terminology issue. It’s bound to happen since two distinct groups have had similar names.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen the Steering Council officially sanctioned a group to set direction for the docs, it used the term “working group.” Later, another documentation working group was set up, but it was focused on more tactical work. The original working group for documentation is now called the Editorial Board.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe now have two groups:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe Documentation Working Group is a community of volunteers contributing to the documentation.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe Editorial Board is a more formal group of decision makers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDoes that clear it up?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2023-10-23T14:17:22.229Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":110,"readers_count":109,"score":72.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":36710,"topic_slug":"pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board","display_username":"Joanna Jablonski","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":3061,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board/36710/7","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":122811,"name":"Hugo van Kemenade","username":"hugovk","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/hugovk/{size}/14505_2.png","created_at":"2023-10-23T14:58:56.359Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThank you! Yes, now I get it:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOld WG → new EB\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOld Docs Community → new WG\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe had been calling group 1 the “Documentation Community Team” in our monthly meetings, for the community of volunteers:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://docs-community.readthedocs.io/en/latest/community/index.html\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eDocumentation Community Team - Documentation Community documentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://docs-community.readthedocs.io/en/latest/monthly-meeting/index.html\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eMonthly Reports Archive - Documentation Community documentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd group 2 was called the “CPython Documentation Workgroup” for the initial formal group of decision makers:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://docs-community.readthedocs.io/en/latest/workgroup/workgroup_charter.html\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eCPython Documentation Workgroup - Documentation Community documentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI think two things might help:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor continuity, we keep the name of “Documentation Community Team” (or similar) for the community of volunteers contributing to the documentation (group 1). Avoiding “working group” for this looser group would avoid confusion with the original working group, which had a charter and membership votes and so on. Similarly with \u003ca href=\"https://www.python.org/psf/workgroups/\"\u003ePSF Work Groups\u003c/a\u003e. Anyone can join in group 1: just turn up and get stuck in.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdate the info at \u003ca href=\"https://docs-community.readthedocs.io/en/latest/workgroup/workgroup_charter.html\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eCPython Documentation Workgroup - Documentation Community documentation\u003c/a\u003e to say the old WG is now the EB (could be mostly deleted and point to this PEP instead). Can of course wait until the PEP is accepted.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2023-10-23T14:58:56.359Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":191,"reads":115,"readers_count":114,"score":1048.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":36710,"topic_slug":"pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board","display_username":"Hugo van Kemenade","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://docs-community.readthedocs.io/en/latest/workgroup/workgroup_charter.html","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"CPython Documentation Workgroup - Documentation Community documentation","clicks":7},{"url":"https://www.python.org/psf/workgroups/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Work Groups of the Python Software Foundation | Python Software Foundation","clicks":3},{"url":"https://docs-community.readthedocs.io/en/latest/community/index.html","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Documentation Community Team - Documentation Community documentation","clicks":2},{"url":"https://docs-community.readthedocs.io/en/latest/monthly-meeting/index.html","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Monthly Reports Archive - Documentation Community documentation","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":358,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board/36710/8","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":132429,"name":"Thomas Wouters","username":"thomas","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/thomas/{size}/5492_2.png","created_at":"2023-12-11T14:39:19.372Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThe SC has decided to accept PEP 732 (The Python Documentation Editorial Board). Our only comment is that while we don’t disagree with the scoping set out in the PEP, it would probably make sense for the EB to consider expanding the scope to include docstrings (in the standard library) once the Board is sufficiently established and the higher priorities have been taken care of. That can be discussed between the EB and SC when the time comes, however.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2023-12-11T14:39:19.372Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":851,"reads":97,"readers_count":96,"score":4474.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":36710,"topic_slug":"pep-732-the-python-documentation-editorial-board","display_username":"Thomas Wouters","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_co